notes = "(!) Extract openmsx-system.zip from the releases into the system folder, so that it ends up as system/openmsx/share: openMSX's machines, extensions and the C-BIOS ROMs. Games then start without any other BIOS.|(!) A real MSX machine (core option System > Machine) needs its system ROMs in system/openmsx/share/systemroms; without them the core starts C-BIOS MSX2+.|(!) The video driver has to be gl.|(!) Disk images need a machine with a disk drive; the C-BIOS machines have none.|(!) A savestate loads only into the build of the core that made it."
description = "openMSX, the MSX emulator that aims for perfection, as a libretro core. It emulates the MSX1, MSX2, MSX2+ and turbo R computers, with C-BIOS machines that need no other BIOS and many real machines with their own ROMs, and extensions such as Konami's SCC, the FM-PAC, MSX-Audio, MoonSound and the GFX9000. Drawn with OpenGL; MSX joystick, cursor keys or mouse per port, the keyboard, savestates, disk swapping and 50 Hz machines."
